# Chaos: the purchased wings of pair 83 sit by their anchor tile and lift their wearer (O747; client/BASE.md "0209"; src/client/chaospiece.h
# (new, pure), outfit.cpp, outfit.h, creature.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp; after 0001-0208).
# Owner 2026-11-24: "Pode importar, com levitação e camada nova." The pack wings (client/tools/sprites/gen_wst_wear.py) were drawn for a
# wearer standing in the anchor tile of their picture, and they lift that wearer: per frame an offset of the body. A wings look with a
# row of chaospiece.h (setOutfitPackPiece, from client_chaos_wingfit/wear_pieces.lua) is placed with its anchor tile on the wearer's
# tile (the creature's place minus the body's displacement), not by the torso measure of 0204 nor the table of 0193; it plays its
# frames at 83 ms; the body (and the head / cape layer of 0210) is drawn at its place plus the lift of that frame
# (setOutfitWingsLift); the wings stay (they rise inside their frames). No stock GameWingOffset lift and no bounce for such a
# wing, no lift on a mount. Creature::draw takes the lift out of the soft shadow's place (0155), so the shadow stays on the ground.
# A wings look without a row, and every other look, draws as before.
